    "body": "## Summary\n- add a configurable live-tracking sanity guard that rejects impossible courier jumps before they corrupt current map state or ETA\n- account for the reported accuracy of both GPS samples before calculating implied movement speed\n- wire the guard into the transactional tracking update path while preserving first-sample and out-of-order handling\n- add unit coverage for first sample, plausible movement, GPS accuracy allowance, and impossible teleport rejection\n- expose the threshold through Spring config, Docker Compose and `.env.example`\n- document the integrity/privacy behavior in the location architecture guide\n\n## Default\n`TRACKING_MAX_IMPLIED_SPEED_METERS_PER_SECOND=80` (~288 km/h). This is intentionally a coarse integrity guard, not fraud detection.\n\n## Validation\nLocal cloning is unavailable in the automation runtime because DNS resolution for github.com fails. GitHub-hosted CI must pass before merge; this PR should remain unmerged if any check fails.",
